The owner's rule explicitly departs from protocol 2.3(b) for clause 4: when clauses 1–3 are cleared and no implementation record or model shows a collapse *caused by a parameter adjustment*, clause 4 is cleared. My closed-book survey of the Ostrom literature (Ostrom 1990; Cox et al. 2010; subsequent case studies) finds no documented instance where a collapse was caused by the collective-choice adjustment process itself. Collapses occur when design principles are absent, incomplete, or overwhelmed by exogenous shocks—not from the adjustment mechanism. Since clauses 1–3 are cleared and the record contains no adjustment-caused collapse, the rule clears clause 4.

All four clauses are now cleared → verdict 1.0.

